  "id": "craniofacial-anomaly",
  "term": "craniofacial anomaly",
  "definition": "A craniofacial anomaly is a congenital difference affecting the skull and face. In this packet, it refers to conditions such as cleft lip and/or cleft palate, which result from incomplete fusion of the lip or roof of the mouth during embryonic development.",
